Cast the sigjmp_buf through void ** so clang accepts __builtin_setjmp / __builtin_longjmp.

THE FAILURE

    src/common/pg_get_line.c:129:30: error: incompatible pointer types passing
        'sigjmp_buf' (aka 'long long[5]') to parameter of type 'void **'
      129 |   if (prompt_ctx && sigsetjmp(*((sigjmp_buf *) prompt_ctx->jmpbuf), 1) != 0)
    src/include/c.h:1343:41: note: expanded from macro 'sigsetjmp'
     1343 | #define sigsetjmp(x,y) __builtin_setjmp(x)

WHY

c.h selects its setjmp mechanism on __MINGW64__, which the mingw-w64 HEADERS define rather than
the compiler, so a clang build follows the same branch as a GCC build. GCC's __builtin_setjmp
takes void *, and an intptr_t[5] decays to a pointer it accepts; clang's signature is void **,
so the same call is rejected.

WHY A CAST AND NOT THE OTHER BRANCH

The tempting alternative is to send clang down the #else branch, where sigjmp_buf becomes the
platform jmp_buf and sigsetjmp becomes the platform setjmp. Upstream rules that out in the
comment three lines above this hunk:

     * that MinGW-64 has some longstanding issues in its setjmp support,
     * so on that toolchain we cheat and use gcc's builtins.

Using the builtins is a deliberate choice for this toolchain, not an accident, so the patch keeps
it and fixes only the argument type.

VERIFIED, not assumed. The concern with the builtins under clang is that __builtin_setjmp lowers
to llvm.eh.sjlj.setjmp, and SJLJ is not the exception model of Windows x86_64. A standalone probe
settles it: with this cast, clang 22.1.8 targeting x86_64-w64-windows-gnu compiles the pair, and
the resulting binary takes the longjmp path and exits 0. The same probe under GCC 15.2.0 behaves
identically, with and without the cast -- intptr_t[5] converts to void ** and then to void *
without complaint -- so the cast is unconditional rather than guarded on __clang__, and the GCC
build is unaffected.

siglongjmp becomes function-like for the same reason: as a bare alias it would hit the identical
argument-type error at its first use.

--- a/src/include/c.h
+++ b/src/include/c.h
@@ -1340,8 +1340,8 @@
 #ifdef WIN32
 #ifdef __MINGW64__
 typedef intptr_t sigjmp_buf[5];
-#define sigsetjmp(x,y) __builtin_setjmp(x)
-#define siglongjmp __builtin_longjmp
+#define sigsetjmp(x,y) __builtin_setjmp((void **) (x))
+#define siglongjmp(x,y) __builtin_longjmp((void **) (x), (y))
 #else							/* !__MINGW64__ */
 #define sigjmp_buf jmp_buf
 #define sigsetjmp(x,y) setjmp(x)
